<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Midrand growth boosts Samrand net.</title>
<headline>Midrand growth boosts Samrand net.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>10 months to Dec 31, 1996, vs year ended Feb 29, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     3.6	   vs 18.3</p>
<p>    Net income		4.60	  vs 0.94</p>
<p>    Income from associate 3.43	  vs 0.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.27	  vs 0.12 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.10	  vs 0.20</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   2.19	  vs  -</p>
<p>    Turnover		  12.34	 vs 0.13</p>
<p>Full name: Samrand Development Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company's year end has been changed and it said reults were not comparable with the previous period due to restructuring.</p>
<p>The property development company said it was benefiting from the rapid growth of Midrand, between Johannesburg and Pretoria.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
